    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1095">

                <pb facs="1000" n="992" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg992"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611b.9417/337</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Philippine
                        A fairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of a Conversation With the Counselor of the Japanese Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Morishima</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-04">June 4, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Morishima called to inform me that his Embassy had been instructed by the
                    Japanese Government to say that the Association of <pb facs="1001" n="993"
                        xml:id="pg993"/> Japanese Exporters of Cotton Piece Goods desired a renewal
                    for <hi rendition="#italic">two</hi> years of the existing agreement limiting
                    the importation of Japanese cotton textiles into the Philippines<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d1095-f1"/> to 45,000,000 square meters per annum. He said that his
                    Government was very anxious to have the renewal made for <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >two</hi> years in order to avoid having the question brought up so often.
                    He thought that it would be to the best interests of both the American and
                    Japanese textile manufacturers to have the situation stabilized for a period at
                    least that long.</p>
                <p>I told Mr. Morishima that I would place the matter before those concerned and
                    communicate with him later.</p>
                <closer><signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oseph</hi>] E. J[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">acobs</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
